// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// NEIGHBORHOOD DIRECTORY — دليل الحي
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Persistent directory of fixed local places (pharmacy, supermarket,
// car wash, etc.). Distinct from Services / Marketplace / Home
// Businesses, which model PEOPLE / accounts. A PlaceListing models
// a PLACE. The two are connected through an optional
// claimedByUserId — a User may claim/manage a PlaceListing, and a
// claimed user's ServiceItems can be rendered on the place detail.
//
// MVP behavior:
//  - Submissions land in PENDING until a NEIGHBORHOOD_MOD / admin
//    reviews them (or VISIBLE_UNVERIFIED if the neighborhood has
//    no active mods — handled at the API layer, not the schema).
//  - imageUrls is stored but NEVER written by API in MVP. Reserved
//    for Phase 1.5 image-upload wiring.
//  - createdByUser is NEVER exposed in public API responses.
//  - COMMUNITY_VERIFIED is intentionally NOT in this enum; reserved
//    for Phase 1.5 alongside the PlaceConfirmation model.

enum PlaceCategory {
  RESTAURANT_CAFE
  PHARMACY
  SUPERMARKET
  CAR_WASH
  LAUNDRY
  CLINIC
  SCHOOL_KINDERGARTEN
  QURAN_CIRCLE
  GAS_STATION
  SHOP_SERVICES
  GYM_CENTER
  SALON
  RESTHOUSE_HALL
  OTHER
}

enum PlaceStatus {
  PENDING               // submitted, awaiting mod review
  VISIBLE_UNVERIFIED    // visible publicly but flagged "غير مؤكد"
  MOD_VERIFIED          // mod-confirmed accuracy
  CLAIMED_BY_OWNER      // owner verified via PlaceClaimRequest
  REJECTED              // mod rejected submission with reason
  REMOVED               // mod-removed a previously-visible place
}

// Where a listing's data originated. LOCAL = added/typed by a
// neighbor. GOOGLE = pulled from Google Places at add-time (rating,
// hours, photos snapshot). Drives the source-attribution badge —
// Google data MUST be attributed per Google's Places ToS.
enum PlaceSource {
  LOCAL
  GOOGLE
}

enum PlaceClaimStatus {
  PENDING
  APPROVED
  REJECTED
  CANCELLED
}

enum PlaceReportType {
  WRONG_INFO
  CLOSED
  DUPLICATE
  WRONG_LOCATION
  WRONG_PHONE
  SPAM
  OTHER
}

enum PlaceReviewStatus {
  VISIBLE
  HIDDEN_BY_MOD
  DELETED_BY_USER
}

model PlaceListing {
  id              String        @id @default(cuid())

  neighborhoodId  String
  neighborhood    Neighborhood  @relation(fields: [neighborhoodId], references: [id])

  name            String
  // NFKC + zero-width strip + lowercase. Written by the API on
  // create/edit so the dupe-detection index works without a Postgres
  // extension. See src/lib/places/normalize.ts.
  nameNormalized  String
  category        PlaceCategory
  description     String?
  phone           String?
  whatsapp        String?
  website         String?
  // Social handles — keep one column per platform to match the
  // User.providerStatus model (User.socialLinks is JSON for
  // historical reasons; new tables use explicit columns so we
  // can index / migrate per platform if needed). Stored as the
  // raw handle ("@hai") or a full https:// URL; the renderer
  // builds the right deep-link.
  instagram       String?
  snapchat        String?
  tiktok          String?
  x               String?  // X / Twitter
  mapUrl          String?
  latitude        Float?
  longitude       Float?
  addressText     String?
  openingHours    String?

  // Owner-editable status pill. Overrides the auto open/closed
  // pill (derived from openingHours + Asia/Riyadh wall clock)
  // whenever set. Predefined option list lives in the UI; the
  // column itself is just a freeform string (≤60 chars validated
  // server-side) so future presets can ship without a migration.
  // Examples: "خارج الخدمة مؤقتًا", "تحت الصيانة", "مزدحم الآن",
  // "مغلق نهائيًا", or any custom owner-supplied text.
  manualStatus      String?
  // Optional auto-clear date. When set AND the timestamp is in
  // the past, readers ignore manualStatus and fall back to the
  // auto pill. We do NOT write to the DB during render to clear
  // expired values — the next PATCH from the owner or a future
  // batch can clean those up. Lazy by design.
  manualStatusUntil DateTime?

  // Reserved for Phase 1.5 image-upload wiring. The MVP API
  // unconditionally strips this from incoming bodies; rows ship
  // with the [] default. Detail-page rendering already handles
  // a non-empty array so no template changes will be needed when
  // we enable the feature.
  imageUrls       String[]      @default([])

  status          PlaceStatus   @default(PENDING)

  // Submitter — NEVER exposed in public API responses (only mod
  // detail + self-view-of-mine). See src/lib/places/serialize.ts
  // for the public-response shape.
  createdByUserId String?
  createdByUser   User?         @relation("PlacesCreated", fields: [createdByUserId], references: [id])

  // Approved claimant — visible publicly with limited fields
  // (id, name, avatarUrl, providerStatus) on the detail page.
  claimedByUserId String?
  claimedByUser   User?         @relation("PlacesClaimed", fields: [claimedByUserId], references: [id])

  // Last mod who acted on this place (approve, reject, edit, remove).
  verifiedByModId String?
  verifiedByMod   User?         @relation("PlacesVerified", fields: [verifiedByModId], references: [id])
  verifiedAt      DateTime?

  rejectionReason String?

  claimRequests   PlaceClaimRequest[]
  reports         PlaceReport[]
  reviews         PlaceReview[]
  contributions   DirectoryContribution[] @relation("PlaceContributions")

  // Denormalized review summary. Recomputed inside the same
  // transaction as every review mutation (create / update /
  // delete / mod-hide) by recalcPlaceRating(); VISIBLE-only.
  // Avg rounded to one decimal (e.g. 4.3). Defaults to 0 / 0
  // so a place with no reviews renders cleanly without a JOIN.
  ratingAvg       Float         @default(0)
  ratingCount     Int           @default(0)

  // ── Google Places provenance + snapshot ──
  // Set when a listing is created from a Google Places pick. The
  // place_id is safe to store indefinitely (Google ToS); the rating/
  // hours/photo snapshot is attribution-required and refreshed via
  // googleSyncedAt (don't treat as permanent — re-sync within ~30d).
  // Photos are stored as Google resource names (refs) only and served
  // through /api/places/photo, never re-hosted (ToS-compliant).
  source            PlaceSource @default(LOCAL)
  googlePlaceId     String?
  googleRating      Float?
  googleRatingCount Int?
  googleHours       String?     // Google weekdayDescriptions, joined by \n (per-day display)
  googlePeriods     Json?       // raw Google opening periods (accurate open/closed pill, handles shifts + per-day variation)
  googlePhotoRefs   String[]    @default([]) // up to 3 photo resource names
  googleReviews     Json?       // up to 5 Google reviews: [{author,rating,text,relativeTime}]
  googleSyncedAt    DateTime?

  createdAt       DateTime      @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime      @updatedAt

  // Browse index (the main /directory query): scope to nbhd +
  // category + visible statuses.
  @@index([neighborhoodId, category, status])
  // Mod-queue index: pending submissions per neighborhood ordered
  // by creation time.
  @@index([neighborhoodId, status, createdAt])
  // Dupe-detection: exact-equality lookup on normalized name +
  // category within the user's neighborhood.
  @@index([neighborhoodId, nameNormalized, category])
  @@index([claimedByUserId])
  @@index([createdByUserId])
}

model PlaceClaimRequest {
  id              String           @id @default(cuid())

  placeId         String
  place           PlaceListing     @relation(fields: [placeId], references: [id])

  userId          String
  user            User             @relation("PlaceClaimsSubmitted", fields: [userId], references: [id])

  message         String?
  // Reserved for Phase 1.5. MVP API strips this; mods review
  // claims on text-message + provider-status signals only.
  evidenceUrls    String[]         @default([])

  status          PlaceClaimStatus @default(PENDING)

  reviewedById    String?
  reviewedBy      User?            @relation("PlaceClaimsReviewed", fields: [reviewedById], references: [id])
  reviewedAt      DateTime?
  rejectionReason String?

  createdAt       DateTime         @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime         @updatedAt

  @@index([placeId, status])
  @@index([userId, status])
}

model PlaceReport {
  id        String          @id @default(cuid())

  placeId   String
  place     PlaceListing    @relation(fields: [placeId], references: [id])

  userId    String
  user      User            @relation("PlaceReportsFiled", fields: [userId], references: [id])

  type      PlaceReportType
  message   String?

  // Lifecycle. PENDING until a mod acts. ACCEPTED = confirmed valid;
  // ACTIONED = a real directory correction was applied (removal / merge /
  // marked-closed / corrected); DISMISSED = invalid/no action. Reputation
  // is awarded (for DUPLICATE/CLOSED only) on ACCEPTED or ACTIONED.
  status        PlaceReportStatus @default(PENDING)
  reviewedById  String?
  reviewedBy    User?           @relation("PlaceReportsReviewed", fields: [reviewedById], references: [id])
  reviewedAt    DateTime?
  reviewNote    String?
  // What correction was applied, when ACTIONED (e.g. "removed",
  // "marked_closed", "merged", "corrected"). Free-form, mod-set.
  actionType    String?

  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())

  @@index([placeId])
  @@index([placeId, status])
  @@index([userId, createdAt])
  @@index([status, createdAt])
}

enum PlaceReportStatus {
  PENDING
  ACCEPTED
  DISMISSED
  ACTIONED
}

// ── Directory reviews ─────────────────────────────────────────
// 1–5 star rating + optional comment from a neighborhood
// resident. One review per (place, user) — POST upserts the
// existing row. Claimed owner can REPLY (single reply, capped
// at 500 chars, snapshot of the replier in ownerReplyByUserId);
// owner CANNOT edit / hide / delete the review itself. Mods can
// hide a review (status flips to HIDDEN_BY_MOD); the user can
// soft-delete their own review (status = DELETED_BY_USER).
// Hidden + deleted rows stay in the table so a hidden-then-
// recreated review can't dodge moderation via the upsert path.
// Aggregates live on PlaceListing.ratingAvg / ratingCount,
// recomputed inside the same transaction as every mutation by
// recalcPlaceRating(); VISIBLE-only.
model PlaceReview {
  id                 String            @id @default(cuid())

  placeId            String
  place              PlaceListing      @relation(fields: [placeId], references: [id])

  userId             String
  user               User              @relation("PlaceReviewsAuthored", fields: [userId], references: [id])

  rating             Int                                                                  // 1..5, server-validated
  body               String?                                                              // max 500 chars

  ownerReplyBody     String?                                                              // max 500 chars
  ownerReplyByUserId String?
  ownerReplyByUser   User?             @relation("PlaceReviewsReplied", fields: [ownerReplyByUserId], references: [id])
  ownerReplyAt       DateTime?

  status             PlaceReviewStatus @default(VISIBLE)
  // Denormalized counter for resident-triggered auto-hide.
  // PlaceReviewReport rows are the source of truth; this is
  // incremented inside the same txn as each report insert so
  // we can threshold-check without a COUNT() on the hot path.
  reportCount        Int               @default(0)
  reports            PlaceReviewReport[]

  createdAt          DateTime          @default(now())
  updatedAt          DateTime          @updatedAt

  @@unique([placeId, userId])
  @@index([placeId, status, createdAt])
  @@index([userId, createdAt])
}

// Resident-filed reports against a PlaceReview. Mirrors the
// post-report shape (Report model) so the UX is familiar and
// mods can later get a unified queue. Auto-hide threshold = 3
// distinct reporters → status flips to HIDDEN_BY_MOD inside
// the same txn as the latest report insert.
//
// Lifecycle: PENDING on insert. Mod dismiss → DISMISSED.
// Mod hide-via-review (or auto-hide threshold trip) →
// ACTION_TAKEN for every PENDING report on that review.
// resolvedAt + resolvedById are the mod-action snapshot.
// We never hard-delete reports — the row is the audit trail.
model PlaceReviewReport {
  id            String        @id @default(cuid())
  reason        ReportReason
  details       String?
  reporter      User          @relation("PlaceReviewReporter", fields: [reporterId], references: [id])
  reporterId    String
  review        PlaceReview   @relation(fields: [reviewId], references: [id])
  reviewId      String
  status        ReportStatus  @default(PENDING)
  resolvedAt    DateTime?
  resolvedById  String?
  resolvedBy    User?         @relation("PlaceReviewReportResolver", fields: [resolvedById], references: [id])
  createdAt     DateTime      @default(now())

  // One report per (reporter, review). The API checks for an
  // existing row before insert so the user sees "أبلغت مسبقاً"
  // instead of a raw DB constraint error.
  @@unique([reporterId, reviewId])
  @@index([reviewId, status])
  // Mod-dashboard query — pending reports ordered by recency.
  @@index([status, createdAt])
}

// ── Service-contact directory ─────────────────────────────────────
// Phone identity is SEPARATED from the public listing so (a) one number
// can back listings in several neighborhoods and (b) a number that
// belongs to a normal app user is never turned into a public profile
// without that user's consent.
//
//   ServiceIdentity         — the phone itself: hashed for dedup/match
//                             (never reversible) + E.164 stored encrypted
//                             at rest when SERVICE_PHONE_KEY is set.
//                             linkedUserId = we MATCHED the phone to a
//                             user (a marker ONLY — never permission to
//                             expose them); ownerUserId = a user who
//                             EXPLICITLY accepted ownership.
//   DirectoryServiceContact — a public listing for that identity in one
//                             neighborhood + category, with display data.
model ServiceIdentity {
  id            String   @id @default(cuid())
  // HMAC-SHA256(e164, pepper) — the dedup / match key. Not reversible.
  phoneHash     String   @unique
  // E.164, AES-256-GCM encrypted when SERVICE_PHONE_KEY is set (plaintext
  // fallback otherwise). Decrypted server-side only when building a
  // PUBLIC contact card (community contacts display the number).
  phoneEnc      String

  // Set when the phone matched an existing app user. PRIVACY: a match
  // marker ONLY — must NEVER expose the user's name/profile or the fact
  // that the number is theirs.
  linkedUserId  String?
  linkedUser    User?    @relation("ServiceIdentityLinked", fields: [linkedUserId], references: [id])
  // Set only when that user EXPLICITLY accepted ownership.
  ownerUserId   String?
  ownerUser     User?    @relation("ServiceIdentityOwner", fields: [ownerUserId], references: [id])

  contacts      DirectoryServiceContact[]

  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt     DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([linkedUserId])
  @@index([ownerUserId])
}

model DirectoryServiceContact {
  id                String           @id @default(cuid())

  serviceIdentityId String
  serviceIdentity   ServiceIdentity  @relation(fields: [serviceIdentityId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  neighborhoodId    String
  neighborhood      Neighborhood     @relation(fields: [neighborhoodId], references: [id])

  category          ServiceCategory
  displayName       String
  description       String?          // short description of the service
  whatsapp          Boolean          @default(false) // WhatsApp on the same number
  serviceArea       String?          // free-text area covered ("شمال جدة")
  notes             String?

  source            ServiceContactSource @default(COMMUNITY_ADDED)
  verification      ServiceVerification  @default(UNVERIFIED)
  status            ServiceContactStatus @default(ACTIVE)

  // Submitter — NEVER exposed in public API responses.
  createdByUserId   String?
  createdByUser     User?            @relation("ServiceContactsCreated", fields: [createdByUserId], references: [id])

  // Audit: when the number was extracted from a post/comment, keep the
  // origin id (not exposed publicly) so abuse can be traced back.
  sourcePostId      String?
  sourceCommentId   String?

  reportCount       Int              @default(0)
  reports           ServiceContactReport[]

  // Denormalized community-review summary. 0/0 renders cleanly, no JOIN.
  ratingAvg         Float            @default(0)
  ratingCount       Int              @default(0)

  createdAt         DateTime         @default(now())
  updatedAt         DateTime         @updatedAt

  // Dedup: one listing per identity per (neighborhood, category). The
  // SAME identity may appear in multiple neighborhoods (separate rows).
  @@unique([serviceIdentityId, neighborhoodId, category])
  @@index([neighborhoodId, category, status])
  @@index([neighborhoodId, status, createdAt])
  @@index([serviceIdentityId])
  @@index([createdByUserId])
}

model ServiceContactReport {
  id        String                     @id @default(cuid())

  contactId String
  contact   DirectoryServiceContact    @relation(fields: [contactId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  userId    String
  user      User                       @relation("ServiceContactReportsFiled", fields: [userId], references: [id])

  reason    ServiceContactReportReason
  message   String?

  createdAt DateTime                   @default(now())

  // One report per (reporter, contact).
  @@unique([contactId, userId])
  @@index([contactId])
  @@index([userId, createdAt])
}

// How the listing entered the directory.
enum ServiceContactSource {
  COMMUNITY_ADDED   // مضاف من السكان
  OWNER_SUBMITTED   // submitted by the number's owner
}

// Trust ladder for a service contact (independent of moderation status).
enum ServiceVerification {
  UNVERIFIED                  // غير موثق
  PENDING_OWNER_CONFIRMATION  // بانتظار تأكيد صاحب الرقم (matched a user)
  CLAIMED                     // owner accepted ownership
  VERIFIED                    // owner completed verification → "مزود خدمة موثق"
}

// Moderation / visibility status.
enum ServiceContactStatus {
  ACTIVE          // publicly visible
  PENDING_REVIEW  // queued (moderation OR owner-confirmation) — not public
  HIDDEN          // auto-hidden after reports / mod-hidden
  REMOVED         // mod-removed
}

// Service trades — distinct from PlaceCategory (place TYPES) because a
// service contact is about WHAT the person does, not a venue type.
enum ServiceCategory {
  PLUMBER          // سباك
  ELECTRICIAN      // كهربائي
  CARPENTER        // نجار
  PAINTER          // دهان
  AC_TECH          // فني تكييف
  CLEANING         // عمالة نظافة
  MOVING           // نقل عفش
  TUTOR            // مدرّس / تأسيس
  TAILOR           // خياط
  HOME_FOOD        // طبخ منزلي / أسر منتجة
  CAR_SERVICE      // خدمة سيارات متنقلة
  TECH_REPAIR      // صيانة أجهزة
  HEALTH_HOME      // خدمات صحية منزلية
  OTHER            // أخرى
}

// Report reasons specific to service contacts (people/phone-based),
// distinct from PlaceReportType which is venue-oriented.
enum ServiceContactReportReason {
  WRONG_PHONE       // رقم غير صحيح
  NOT_THIS_PERSON   // لا يخص هذا الشخص
  FRAUD_OR_ABUSE    // احتيال أو إزعاج
  INAPPROPRIATE     // محتوى غير مناسب
}

// ── Directory contributions + reputation events ───────────────────
// A reviewable record of a user's directory contribution. Reputation is
// awarded ONLY when status flips to APPROVED — never on submit, never on
// REJECTED/DUPLICATE/NEEDS_EDIT. Existing PlaceListing/PlaceReport flows
// keep working; a contribution row rides alongside for reward tracking.
model DirectoryContribution {
  id              String                      @id @default(cuid())
  type            DirectoryContributionType
  status          DirectoryContributionStatus @default(PENDING_REVIEW)

  contributorId   String
  contributor     User                        @relation("DirectoryContributions", fields: [contributorId], references: [id])

  // Set for contributions tied to an existing/new place row.
  placeId         String?
  place           PlaceListing?               @relation("PlaceContributions", fields: [placeId], references: [id])
  neighborhoodId  String
  neighborhood    Neighborhood                @relation(fields: [neighborhoodId], references: [id])

  payloadJson     Json?
  // Flagged at create-time when a near-duplicate place exists (name +
  // category + proximity in the same neighborhood). Surfaced in review.
  potentialDuplicate Boolean                  @default(false)

  reviewNote      String?
  reviewedById    String?
  reviewedBy      User?                       @relation("DirectoryContributionsReviewed", fields: [reviewedById], references: [id])
  reviewedAt      DateTime?

  createdAt       DateTime                    @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime                    @updatedAt

  @@index([neighborhoodId, status, createdAt])
  @@index([contributorId, createdAt])
  @@index([placeId])
}

// Idempotent, audited reputation grant. Unique (sourceType, sourceId)
// guarantees a given source can only ever award once — re-approving a
// contribution can't double-pay. Separate from the social `reputationLog`
// (different cap + no idempotency); both increment User.reputation.
model ReputationEvent {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId      String
  user        User     @relation("ReputationEvents", fields: [userId], references: [id])
  sourceType  String   // e.g. "directory_contribution"
  sourceId    String   // the contribution id
  points      Int
  reason      String   // a ReputationReason value (see lib/reputation/directoryRewards)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())

  @@unique([sourceType, sourceId])
  @@index([userId, createdAt])
}

enum DirectoryContributionType {
  CREATE_PLACE
  EDIT_PLACE
  ADD_PHOTO
  FIX_LOCATION
  ADD_CONTACT
  REPORT_DUPLICATE
  REPORT_CLOSED
}

enum DirectoryContributionStatus {
  PENDING_REVIEW
  APPROVED
  REJECTED
  DUPLICATE
  NEEDS_EDIT
}

// ── Neighborhood pinned reference items ───────────────────────────
// Moderator-pinned references (a message/file/link/post/comment/note) that
// residents can find later without re-asking. Self-contained snapshot
// (title/summary/fileUrl/linkUrl) so it renders even if the source post
// later expires from the feed — pinned-item visibility is INDEPENDENT of
// the source's feed/highlight expiry. Pinning never mutates the source.
model NeighborhoodPinnedItem {
  id              String   @id @default(cuid())

  neighborhoodId  String
  neighborhood    Neighborhood @relation(fields: [neighborhoodId], references: [id])

  type            PinnedItemType
  // Origin reference (null for MANUAL_NOTE/standalone FILE/LINK). The
  // source is loaded on demand by a resolver that can read EXPIRED posts/
  // comments but still respects deletion + moderation removal.
  sourceType      String?   // "post" | "comment" | "message" | "file" | "link"
  sourceId        String?

  title           String
  summary         String?
  fileUrl         String?
  linkUrl         String?

  status          PinnedItemStatus @default(ACTIVE)
  priority        Int      @default(0)   // higher = shown first

  pinnedById      String
  pinnedBy        User     @relation("PinnedItemsPinned", fields: [pinnedById], references: [id])
  pinnedAt        DateTime @default(now())
  expiresAt       DateTime?               // null = forever

  hiddenById      String?
  hiddenBy        User?    @relation("PinnedItemsHidden", fields: [hiddenById], references: [id])
  hiddenAt        DateTime?
  hiddenReason    String?

  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt

  auditLogs       NeighborhoodPinnedItemAuditLog[]

  // Resident browse: nbhd + status + expiry + priority ordering.
  @@index([neighborhoodId, status, expiresAt])
  @@index([neighborhoodId, priority, pinnedAt])
  // Duplicate-pin lookup: at most one pin per source per neighborhood.
  @@unique([neighborhoodId, sourceType, sourceId])
}

model NeighborhoodPinnedItemAuditLog {
  id            String   @id @default(cuid())
  pinnedItemId  String
  pinnedItem    NeighborhoodPinnedItem @relation(fields: [pinnedItemId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  actorId       String
  actor         User     @relation("PinnedItemAuditActor", fields: [actorId], references: [id])
  action        PinnedItemAction
  oldValueJson  Json?
  newValueJson  Json?
  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([pinnedItemId, createdAt])
}

enum PinnedItemType {
  POST
  COMMENT
  MESSAGE
  FILE
  LINK
  MANUAL_NOTE
}

enum PinnedItemStatus {
  ACTIVE
  HIDDEN
  EXPIRED
  REMOVED
}

enum PinnedItemAction {
  PIN
  UPDATE
  HIDE
  UNHIDE
  EXPIRE
  REMOVE
  REORDER
}
